# The Wonrich topic set (SCRUM-88). One line per topic: name:partitions:retention-ms
#
# This file is the single definition of the topics. create-topics.sh reads it for local
# development and infra/azure/eventhubs.sh reads it when provisioning staging, so the two cannot
# drift apart by someone editing one and forgetting the other.
#
# Naming: wonrich.<owning service>.<event in plural>.v<schema version>
# See docs/kafka.md for why, and for what a version bump means.
#
# Partitions: 3 on the event topics. Partition count is the ceiling on how many consumers in one
# group can read in parallel, and it can be raised later but never lowered. Three is enough for
# this system and still orders events per key.
#
# Retention: 7 days on event topics - long enough that a consumer down over a weekend catches up,
# short enough to stay inside the free tiers. Dead-letter topics keep 30 days, because a message
# lands there precisely when nobody was watching and it needs to survive until someone looks.

wonrich.intake.lab-results.v1:3:604800000
wonrich.processing.stage-events.v1:3:604800000
wonrich.processing.hold-events.v1:3:604800000

# One dead-letter topic per consumer group, not per source topic: what matters when replaying is
# which consumer failed to handle the message, since that is the code being fixed.
# Single partition - dead letters are rare and ordering across them is easier to reason about.
wonrich.dlq.processing-lab-results.v1:1:2592000000
wonrich.dlq.processing-stage-events.v1:1:2592000000
wonrich.dlq.processing-hold-events.v1:1:2592000000

# Quality Lab topics
wonrich.quality-lab.batch-determinations.v1:3:604800000
wonrich.dlq.quality-lab-stage-events.v1:1:2592000000
